From e5057461ca505ee69645d44aafbb381c60c79cdf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 12:07:06 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] desktop: a disproved no-reply notice leaves with its
 turn's reply

The silent-turn check (45 s without events -> session.active_list) read a
running hub turn as ended and stamped "Hermes ended this turn without a
reply". The turn then finished and its reply was stored, but the refresh
kept the stamped bubble as a second one under the reply, with a Retry that
would have re-run the prompt (chat 20261111_055255_6e01c3, 2026-11-17).

- reconciliation: a no-reply notice whose turn has a stored reply is
  cleared before local error bubbles are preserved or folded, matched by
  descriptor or by text (the incident's bubble had lost its descriptor).
- liveTurnVerdict / liveTurnLastActiveMs: fall back to the row whose
  session_key is the chat's stored id when no row carries the runtime id.
- every silent-turn check writes one [silent-turn] line to desktop.log
  (row matched or not, status, idle seconds); a wrong "ended" left no trace.

Not established: which snapshot answer (row missing vs idle) produced the
wrong verdict on the hub. The log line is what will name it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
